WEBVTT

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.520
Lauren, I finished.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:47.910
Warren!

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:24.800
children you're a great help come here come here Corky Corky what are you doing you come out of here out

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.090
Now, Crocky, don't get in the way.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.130
Off you go and be careful.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:38.940
Careful.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:39.990
Thanks, Mom.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:40.810
Bye, teacher.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:41.230
Oh, Mom.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.860
We'll bring our presents this afternoon.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:43.610
Bye, children.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:06:00.000
Children, see them.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:00.640
as it is.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.320
Good morning, dear.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.400
Good morning, Walter.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:07.880
Everything packed?

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.120
I think so, but I'll probably get home and find I've left behind me all that's really

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:13.560
important.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.500
And I'm going to miss you.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.060
Thanks.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:17.300
Well, let me see.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:18.770
Hardly no way to begin.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:19.670
The place is such a muggle.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:21.430
Let's go finish this.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.650
I never did like these rugs anyway.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:24.810
I think I'll get some new ones.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.230
Oh, I don't know.

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:28.890
Here, see?

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.000
Pull it on that side.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.550
Now, there must be some system to this.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.670
Now, you can stand on them and I can sweep.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.130
And we both wind up on the floor.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:38.970
No, thanks.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.470
Besides, you'll be late for your train.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.350
Are you watching the time?

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:42.710
Yes, I'm ready to try.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.370
And I hate waiting rooms.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.010
Well, you can't sit around.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:49.510
Why do you suppose I'd wait a few to go on your vacation before I start a cleaning house?

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:53.570
You're the most disorganized woman I ever knew.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.790
You think you'll ever get all this back together again?

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:57.450
I hope so.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:58.730
I have a man coming to help me.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:06:59.510
Good.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:11.870
What's the sense in dusting all of them? Seems to me you make a lot of extra work for

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:12.910
yourself.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:17.290
Why don't you have each person who wants to read a book dust it himself?

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.380
Morning Ruth.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.150
Helen.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:24.340
Morning Ruth.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.660
This place.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.000
I thought you were gone on your own.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:37.480
vacation she put me to work why are you here so early i'm being punished dad and mother went over

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:42.500
to the ellisons for the day so i'm supposed to help you on a saturday too don't tell me you're

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:50.090
out late again last night but after all you went through with your mother last week i'm not a child

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:56.460
look who's not a child lots of girls my age are married and have children oh i wouldn't say lots

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:00.000
had your breakfast yes thanks good then supporting you get right

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:00.560
to work.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.800
Don't I even get a chance

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:02.600
to catch my bread?

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:03.360
No, you can do that

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:04.140
while you dust the shade.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:07.970
Oh, my.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.010
It's late then, wait.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.620
Ruth, dear,

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.080
exactly how long

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:23.900
did your mother say

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.160
I was to punish you today?

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:26.780
Just work me to the bone,

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:27.440
I suppose.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:28.180
I see.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:29.910
Well, great, we're going.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.440
I don't think we'll get to the bone till next fall.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:36.850
Just 'cause I was out late last night.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:41.640
Parents are so insensitive.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.460
We had such a beautiful evening planned.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:49.640
I'll never be able to face Tom when he finds out I've been ordered to stay home tonight, just like a child.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.150
Tom, no.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.470
Oh, dear, whatever happened to Larry?

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.620
I thought he was the big love of your life.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.460
Larry just wasn't for me.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.190
I found that out when I met Tom.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.060
- You've been out of touch with men for so long, Aunt Helen.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.320
You wouldn't understand.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.000
- Oh, I don't know.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.210
My poor old memory isn't that dim.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.380
Oh, I wonder if I've got everything.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:17.580
Um, Ruth, I really don't think you ought to stay here

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.560
and help me anymore today.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.280
- You mean I can go home?

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.100
- No, come here.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.980
I want you to deliver these packages to the school

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.160
for the party this evening.

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:27.500
Nice lot of them.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.870
See that you deliver them.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:34.760
When you've finished, I want you to drop this box of old clothes at the church for me.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.360
I guess everybody wants me to die of exhaustion.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.560
Don't you think that's too much to ask a woman of her advanced age?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.760
Guess this will fill up my whole day.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.340
Oh, no, I want you to come back when you're through.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:47.560
Perhaps by then I'll have found a large wash for you to do or something.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.820
That's sweet of you.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.000
Goodbye, Mr. Armstrong.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.140
I hope you have a nice Christmas.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.240
Thanks, Ruthie, and goodbye.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.000
Oh, peace at last.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.630
It is nice, isn't it?

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:02.550
Oh, yes.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.910
Now I can finish the rest of my Christmas packages.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:05.930
I've, uh...

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:06.270
Yes?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.450
I have something to straighten out with you.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:13.050
Now this, this should take care of my room for two more weeks, shouldn't it?

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.260
And as I told you, if Mr. Frank shows up, you can let him have it while I'm away.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.600
Then you won't be alone in the house.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:20.980
I'll be all right, thanks.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.310
Well, I don't expect any telephone calls.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:28.960
You have my phone in the address, and I'm going to miss that room.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:31.470
Ned liked that room, too.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.490
He kept writing about how much he missed it while he was in the service.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.460
Heavens, what time is it?

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:43.680
Oh, plenty of time.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:44.760
Nearly an hour.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.380
You're not that early and you know it.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.000
Now hurry along or you'll really be late.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:50.100
Oh, all right.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.680
I wish I could send you a box of snow from where I'm going.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:07.580
So do I.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:08.660
Oh, let me help you.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:12.890
Well, I haven't heard Corky bark in ages.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.250
I wonder what's the matter with him.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.860
He decided he's going to be a watchdog.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.180
He's the man I hired.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:35.290
You know, I believe he's afraid of Corky.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.290
He couldn't be.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.290
Now, hurry or you're going to miss that train.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.650
Corky, you bad dog.

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:42.150
Come here.

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:43.550
Boy, I'm sorry.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.550
I don't know what's come over him.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.440
Glad you're here.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:47.440
The name is...

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.440
Howard Wilton, ma'am.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.440
Oh, that's right.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.440
Howard Wilton, Mr. Armstrong.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:51.440
I'm glad to meet you.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.390
I know you're going to be a great help, Mr. Gordon.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:54.390
I hope to be.

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.400
I tried to make friends with him.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.400
Oh, he just doesn't trust strangers.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.400
I'm sorry.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.000
Nice meeting you.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:01.900
Goodbye, Ellen.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:02.640
Goodbye, dear.

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.880
And drop me a card, won't you?

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.000
I'll do that.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:07.160
Goodbye, Corky.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:07.720
Bye.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.000
See him off to the gate, Corky.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:09.360
Go on.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:10.470
Oh, my.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.410
Sorry I'm late.

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:13.530
Oh, that's all right.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.380
So much to do.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:16.600
Oh, yes, the weed.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:17.260
Here.

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:18.540
Thank you.

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:20.330
Where does it go?

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:21.570
Right over the door.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.970
The dog wasn't here when I came yesterday.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:26.590
No.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.450
He runs off all the time.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:30.000
Let me see.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.820
seen a dog yet that liked me. You probably imagine they don't like you. That looks nice.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:42.010
Have you ever owned one? No. Better come inside and get started now.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.950
Give me your coat and I'll hang it here in the closet.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:22.020
Put this.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:25.500
Oh, I'll take it.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.590
Now, let me see.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.920
Oh, yes, I think I'd like the floors waxed first.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:35.330
floors are my specialty. Maybe I don't work as fast as others, but when I finish, you know

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:50.920
they've really been polished. That's good. Well, I'll get the waxing things. Carry that.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.820
It's too heavy. Thank you. You should let me get it. Oh, I'm used to carrying it. Well, you won't

00:13:54.820 --> 00:14:00.000
carry it anymore. Now, uh, oh, yes. Why don't you put the rye on?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.000
on the front lawn, then they'll be out of your way.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:02.720
All right.

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:42.710
- Need me help, Mrs. Gordy? - Boxes.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.480
Gordon, if you don't mind, I'd like to take my coat somewhere else.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:03.700
Yes, you see, I didn't know it was a storage closet.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:05.830
It might get dirty.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.330
It's my only coat.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:12.960
Oh, well, I have a cedar closet upstairs.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:14.740
You can put it there if you like.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:15.480
Yes.

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:17.640
As soon as I get rid of these, I'll take it up.

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:21.390
If you tell me where the closet is, I'll take it up.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.350
Oh, it's the first door on the right at the top of the stairs.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.360
Wouldn't want you running upstairs on my account.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.520
Operator, 4892, please.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:07.650
Yes, thank you.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:12.560
Hello, this is Mrs. Gordon.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:13.840
Would you get Mr. Anderson for me?

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:20.130
Mr. Anderson?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:23.020
I've got quite a Christmas list for you.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.760
Thank you.

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:17.800
Very well, then. I'll expect him.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:19.830
Late this afternoon?

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.980
Oh, thank you. I appreciate it.

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:22.600
Bye.

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.250
Would you like me to help you trim the tree?

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:35.360
Oh, no, thank you.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.840
I just wanted to look at them.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.500
I really think we should get on with the work now.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:41.000
Mrs. Gordon.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:41.820
Yes?

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:46.130
You're not dissatisfied with the work I'm doing, are you?

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:47.130
Why, no.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.590
So far, you're doing very well.

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:55.430
And you weren't telephoning anybody about me, were you?

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:56.360
Why, no.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:57.140
Why should I?

00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:58.620
Besides, who would I call?

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.000
I don't need any reference.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:30.000
preferences. I was just phoning about some groceries. You see, I'm very anxious to make good on this job. I always try to do my best. I work very hard, but nobody realizes it. I get paid, but... Something's troubling you, isn't it?

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.160
Would you like to tell me about it?

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:33.690
No, it's nothing.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.840
Oh, now, haven't you ever been troubled

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.720
and talked things over with one of your friends?

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:46.460
I haven't any friends.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.630
Just because you work for me

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:51.510
is no reason why we can't be friends.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:52.830
Yes, it is.

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:54.050
Why?

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:57.370
Because I'll only be here for today, Mrs. Gordon.

00:20:57.510 --> 00:21:00.000
I'll clean your house, do my job,

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.800
and be gone and forgotten as far as you're concerned and looking for the next job wherever

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:13.590
that is oh no that isn't necessarily true why you might fit in here very nicely i like you you need

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:19.720
the work and i certainly need someone to help me you mean maybe i could come back yes we might even

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:30.000
have a regular day every week perhaps even two oh that'd be fine but it won't work out that way oh

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:30.940
Why not?

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.590
This will be just like all the other jobs.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.380
Most people only have me once.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:38.570
Or at best, twice.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.940
Perhaps they can't afford it.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.120
Why do they have me in the first place?

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:50.020
Please forgive me for saying this.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:51.850
It's really none of my business.

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:55.090
But you know, if you keep things too long within yourself,

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:57.710
you forget how to share your troubles with others.

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:00.000
You shut everyone away from.

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:12.690
you're doing now don't you see what I'm trying to say is I know what it is to be

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:30.000
lonely too better get on with my work of course I didn't mean

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.000
I didn't mean to offend you.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:32.330
I know you didn't.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:36.240
If you need anything, I'll be upstairs.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:37.330
Just call me.

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:39.540
What are you doing here?

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:40.830
Working.

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:42.190
Where's my aunt?

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:43.770
Upstairs.

00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:46.500
Oh, Aunt Helen, I'm back.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:48.020
What do I have to do now?

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:49.310
Nothing, dear.

00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:51.610
Just go home and I'll be in my way.

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:52.470
Thank you.

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:53.020
What?

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:53.890
That's that.

00:23:54.210 --> 00:23:55.100
I'm starved.

00:23:55.310 --> 00:23:55.910
How about you?

00:23:56.110 --> 00:23:56.310
No.

00:23:56.850 --> 00:23:58.000
Want some potato chips?

00:23:59.320 --> 00:23:59.580
No.

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:00.000
No.

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:04.560
I'm glad Aunt Helen finally found herself a nice-looking man to have around the house.

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:06.340
Do you see Mr. Armstrong?

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:07.800
Yes.

00:24:08.140 --> 00:24:09.160
Not much, huh?

00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:11.880
I said to Aunt Helen only the other day,

00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:14.520
if you're going to have a man around, at least have a lively one.

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:18.380
After all, just because you're a widow doesn't mean you have to turn yourself into an old maid.

00:24:19.010 --> 00:24:22.030
Good heavens, Uncle Ned's been dead almost two years.

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:28.030
But I guess once you've been married, you can't ever be an old maid again.

00:24:28.620 --> 00:24:29.400
Not exactly.

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:36.650
I know one thing, Aunt Helen won't be quite so lonely anymore with you around.

00:24:39.080 --> 00:24:42.520
Very talkative, are you?

00:24:45.710 --> 00:24:49.460
Gee, when I see nice, shiny floors like this, I feel like dancing.

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:52.660
Do you like to dance?

00:24:52.860 --> 00:24:53.140
No.

00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:54.500
Do you know how?

00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:55.140
No.

00:24:55.710 --> 00:24:56.630
Maybe you'd like to learn.

00:24:56.910 --> 00:24:57.610
No, I wouldn't.

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:17.510
when I've had less cooperation in my entire life.

