Howard, Howard, I know I've lied to you today.

00:55:15.290 --> 00:55:16.190
I haven't been fair.

00:55:17.250 --> 00:55:19.610
But from now on, I really will do things differently.

00:55:20.550 --> 00:55:23.430
I've been wrong in everything I've done so far.

00:55:24.660 --> 00:55:26.230
It's all been my fault.

00:55:27.470 --> 00:55:28.530
Things really will be different.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.720
Because we understand each other now, don't we?

00:55:32.220 --> 00:55:32.620
Yes.

00:55:33.230 --> 00:55:34.790
There'll be no more trouble.

00:55:35.780 --> 00:55:36.500
No more trouble.

00:55:37.240 --> 00:55:38.660
That's all I've ever wanted.

00:55:40.590 --> 00:55:42.130
Mr. Armstrong's room is yours.

00:55:42.270 --> 00:55:42.990
You can have it.

00:55:44.910 --> 00:55:48.230
But I would like to see if it's tidy for you.

00:55:49.370 --> 00:55:52.000
See, some of the drapes may be a little faded.

00:55:52.310 --> 00:55:55.030
The rug, one of the rug's worn.

00:55:56.360 --> 00:55:58.420
Well, you might even want some of the furniture moved around.

00:55:58.990 --> 00:56:00.000
So I'll just go up.

00:56:00.280 --> 00:56:11.590
Look, I'll be right down, but there's no need for you to come up.

00:56:11.990 --> 00:56:13.540
I told you, I won't be long.

00:56:15.260 --> 00:56:29.260
You're good at fixing up rooms.

00:56:31.210 --> 00:56:34.910
I've never been able to afford much rent, so I had to do the best with what I had.

00:56:37.880 --> 00:56:41.080
I'm sorry.

00:56:43.830 --> 00:56:48.270
It's a nice room.

00:56:50.390 --> 00:56:53.890
Big closet.

00:56:55.450 --> 00:56:56.730
Easier to keep things in order.

00:57:02.750 --> 00:57:17.120
- This is nice too.

00:57:17.120 --> 00:57:19.640
- Army kill.

00:57:19.640 --> 00:57:23.270
- Husbands, store it away.

00:57:40.780 --> 00:57:45.790
our soldiers go to, like your husband.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:00.680
Thank you, husband.

00:58:03.430 --> 00:58:06.720
Here, let me help you take the coat off.

00:58:10.930 --> 00:58:20.240
Please, no.

00:58:20.240 --> 00:58:20.520
No.

00:58:33.870 --> 00:58:35.610
I think I'll change things around.

00:58:37.500 --> 00:58:40.410
Sometimes at night I can't sleep and I like to look out.

00:58:42.820 --> 00:58:44.200
I'll move the bed over by the window.

00:58:48.870 --> 00:58:58.820
Things will be different for me now because you'll help me to forget things that bother me.

00:59:02.940 --> 00:59:03.600
Very grateful.

00:59:12.680 --> 00:59:17.480
Just a trick, is it?

00:59:18.330 --> 00:59:20.980
You're not just saying all these.

00:59:23.070 --> 00:59:25.530
Because if I thought you didn't mean them, I couldn't stand it.

00:59:39.370 --> 00:59:40.150
Someone downstairs.

00:59:40.970 --> 00:59:41.560
Yes.

00:59:42.310 --> 00:59:43.920
We'd better let him in.

00:59:45.700 --> 00:59:46.200
Yes.

01:00:15.740 --> 01:00:16.940
Doug, the grocery boy.

01:00:17.710 --> 01:00:18.980
Better let him in.

01:00:33.260 --> 01:00:34.440
You'll get rid of them quick, won't you?

01:00:36.590 --> 01:00:38.380
Hello, Doug.

01:00:38.680 --> 01:00:40.190
What happened to your window, Mr. Gordon?

01:00:40.810 --> 01:00:42.380
There's glass all over the porch.

01:00:42.480 --> 01:00:43.780
Yes, I know. It was an accident.

01:00:44.610 --> 01:00:45.830
Gee, that's too bad.

01:00:46.900 --> 01:00:47.360
Hi there.

01:00:47.740 --> 01:00:49.010
Doug, this is Howard Wilton.

01:00:49.270 --> 01:00:49.930
Glad to meet you.

01:00:50.090 --> 01:00:52.300
He's working here today.

01:00:52.890 --> 01:00:54.010
See, that's swell.

01:00:54.720 --> 01:00:56.280
Wish I had a job indoors today.

01:00:58.190 --> 01:00:59.030
I'll chill you out.

01:01:01.310 --> 01:01:08.950
she gave me a hot cup of chocolate this morning. I'm sorry. That's all right. Where's Corby,

01:01:09.050 --> 01:01:13.850
Mrs. Gordon? Oh, he ran off this morning. Shouldn't I go look for him? No, thank you.

01:01:14.980 --> 01:01:19.950
My Timmy's a smart dog, Mrs. Gordon. He never strays from our place. You've never seen me,

01:01:20.010 --> 01:01:25.990
have you? No. He's a big dog. And tricks? Not a thing that dog can't do when he puts

01:01:25.990 --> 01:01:30.000
his mind to it. Just yesterday. Yes, yes, I know. Say, are you all right?

01:01:30.670 --> 01:01:34.980
Well, you don't look it. If it's Corky that's worrying you, I'll be glad to take a look for you.

01:01:34.980 --> 01:01:37.870
No, thank you. I just have a sort of a headache, that's all.

01:01:37.870 --> 01:01:41.050
Yeah? Ever heard of holding your breath for a headache?

01:01:41.050 --> 01:01:42.050
No, I haven't.

01:01:42.050 --> 01:01:44.050
Some kids at school were telling me.

01:01:44.050 --> 01:01:46.050
Doug, I'm perfectly all right.

01:01:46.050 --> 01:01:48.930
Mom takes aspirins for hers. If you haven't got any...

01:01:48.930 --> 01:01:51.930
I'm busy today. I have the time to talk.

01:01:51.930 --> 01:01:55.670
You don't have to check. I'm sure it's all there.

01:01:55.670 --> 01:01:57.680
But I've got to, Mrs. Gordon.

01:01:57.680 --> 01:02:00.000
Mr. Anderson says, "All we need is to go."

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:29.570
to be sure. If not all here, it means another trip. Very well. I'll give you a check then. A check? How much is it? Doug, don't argue. How much is it? Four dollars and 37 cents. All right. Say, is she giving you trouble today too? Trouble? Yeah, she's always so nice. I like her better than any of my customers. She's busy. Yeah,

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.800
Why is she taking time out to write a check?

01:02:32.110 --> 01:02:33.750
She always pays at the end of the month.

01:02:35.280 --> 01:02:37.160
I guess she's not going to trade with us anymore.

01:02:38.290 --> 01:02:40.300
Surest, I know if I did something wrong.

01:02:40.560 --> 01:02:50.190
Your money.

01:02:50.470 --> 01:02:52.050
Mrs. Gordon's going to give me a check.

01:02:52.110 --> 01:02:52.570
Never mind.

01:02:52.970 --> 01:02:54.350
But I haven't got change.

01:02:54.640 --> 01:02:55.350
Keep the change.

01:02:55.990 --> 01:02:56.810
Gee, thanks.

01:02:57.190 --> 01:03:00.000
Will you tell Mrs. Gordon that I'm sorry she's not feeling well?

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:01.720
Well, and if there's anything I can do...

01:03:01.720 --> 01:03:03.000
Go along now. We're very busy.

01:03:03.270 --> 01:03:03.670
Sure.

01:03:04.310 --> 01:03:04.830
Well...

01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:42.480
I'm finished now.

01:10:00.760 --> 01:10:03.060
I found this money in the kitchen while I was cleaning up.

01:10:03.610 --> 01:10:04.880
Was it meant for me?

01:10:06.060 --> 01:10:07.410
Yes.

01:10:08.440 --> 01:10:08.920
Thank you.

01:10:10.480 --> 01:10:13.670
I think I'll go home now.

01:10:15.090 --> 01:10:16.380
Very tired.

01:10:22.200 --> 01:10:24.130
It's locked.

01:10:24.960 --> 01:10:27.250
You have the key.

01:10:29.000 --> 01:10:30.000
Why should I have it?

01:10:35.720 --> 01:10:36.540
I have two keys.

01:10:44.080 --> 01:10:45.500
Unlock it.

01:10:49.180 --> 01:10:50.770
Just unlock it.

01:10:57.290 --> 01:11:00.000
Steven from the phone company.

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:02.140
That phone of you has been reported out all day.

01:11:02.510 --> 01:11:05.230
Sorry I couldn't get here any sooner, but we've really been swamped.

01:11:05.290 --> 01:11:06.610
Is your phone out of order, Mrs. Gordon?

01:11:07.270 --> 01:11:08.460
Why, no.

01:11:08.960 --> 01:11:10.360
No, there must be some mistake.

01:11:10.580 --> 01:11:11.460
Well, that's funny.

01:11:12.310 --> 01:11:13.430
I've had several reports.

01:11:14.130 --> 01:11:16.130
Maybe I'd better go and check with Joe in the car.

01:11:16.290 --> 01:11:17.090
Oh, just a minute.

01:11:18.310 --> 01:11:20.040
I wonder, could you do me a favor?

01:11:20.260 --> 01:11:20.600
Certainly.

01:11:21.010 --> 01:11:22.650
This man's been working here all day.

01:11:22.930 --> 01:11:23.990
He's not very well.

01:11:24.470 --> 01:11:25.790
I mean, he's very tired.

01:11:26.390 --> 01:11:28.360
I was wondering, could you drop him at the car line?

01:11:28.360 --> 01:11:29.920
Well, I'd be glad to.

01:11:30.380 --> 01:11:31.160
Thank you very much.

01:11:31.220 --> 01:11:32.260
But I can't wait long.

01:11:32.560 --> 01:11:34.920
Joe and I have another call to make way on the other side of town.

01:11:35.060 --> 01:11:35.900
No, right away.

01:11:36.930 --> 01:11:39.110
Howard, why don't you go out and sit in the car?

01:11:46.270 --> 01:11:49.530
Now that Mr. Stevens is here, I do want him to check the phone to see that all is in order.

01:11:50.070 --> 01:11:51.230
You will do that for me, won't you?

01:11:51.330 --> 01:11:51.850
Sure thing.

01:11:52.830 --> 01:11:54.450
Well, Mr. Stevens will be right, Howard.

01:11:54.880 --> 01:11:55.830
All right, Mrs. Grewick.

01:11:56.870 --> 01:11:58.040
Please, come in.

01:11:59.630 --> 01:11:59.920
Quickly.

01:12:00.160 --> 01:12:01.200
I don't want him to hear us.

01:12:01.810 --> 01:12:03.510
Of course, there's something wrong with the phone.

01:12:03.810 --> 01:12:04.650
He ripped the wires.

01:12:05.190 --> 01:12:05.870
He's insane.

01:12:06.600 --> 01:12:06.960
What?

01:12:07.100 --> 01:12:08.020
He tried to kill me.

01:12:09.090 --> 01:12:10.090
Are you serious?

01:12:10.400 --> 01:12:11.420
Yes, of course I am.

01:12:11.890 --> 01:12:13.250
He's locked me in this house all day.

01:12:14.210 --> 01:12:16.550
I even had to smash one of the kitchen windows to try and get out.

01:12:17.340 --> 01:12:18.780
Oh, please, you've got to believe me.

01:12:19.230 --> 01:12:21.440
Look, come with me and I'll prove it to you.

01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:53.740
- You will get him to the police, won't you? - All right, I guess Joe and I can take care of him.

01:12:53.740 --> 01:12:54.860
Oh, thank you.

01:13:09.560 --> 01:13:18.290
Mrs. Gordon! He's gone, Mrs. Gordon. You better lock yourself inside.

01:13:18.450 --> 01:13:22.390
Oh, no, he can't have gone far. You've got to find him. You've got to.

01:13:22.410 --> 01:13:23.290
All right, but how about you?

01:13:23.370 --> 01:13:24.650
I'll be all right. Just find him.

01:15:01.600 --> 01:15:03.780
It was in your bedroom closet with a sheet over it.

01:15:04.000 --> 01:15:14.370
I want some tickets.

01:15:15.220 --> 01:15:17.760
Tickets to a party.

01:15:19.600 --> 01:15:21.400
Must have picked him up by mistake.

01:15:21.730 --> 01:15:24.840
Must be yours.

01:16:00.670 --> 01:16:04.150
It's Mr. Stevens. It was nice of him to come back.
